{"author":{"id":"U_kgDOFG5Y7w","is_bot":false,"login":"orda-aska","name":"Orda"},"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"38a7072f8d23fe865b4d48d1da285a6db4fc14d1","body":"## Purpose\n\nComplete the evidence collection for #14. This branch preserves the executed trials, negative results, contradictions, raw witnesses, review texts, and exact publication readbacks under `research/iteration-2026-11-21/`.\n\nEvidence head: `516431afa21d53b98265aa8735f8a871707aad98`.\n\nPreregistration: `3e2c8675514fe2d2b6b59706edf73f5cfa8e6273`.\n\nBase: `38a7072f8d23fe865b4d48d1da285a6db4fc14d1`.\n\n## Coverage\n\n- Lane 7 verifier ordering: reproduced acceptance of a candidate digest recorded after evaluation. Verdict `VERIFIED / N1-local` for the defect only.\n- Aletheia tooling: four isolated modes reproduced 13 tests, 13 mutation kills, and one stable audit digest. Verdict `N0`.\n- Frozen contract and bounded controller: 65 repository tests and 11 focused contract tests passed. Combined adversarial integration had 6 passes and 8 failures across 14 checks.\n- Cerebras client: mocked error leakage, timeout accounting, and numeric-boundary defects reproduced. Live provider behavior remains `UNVERIFIED`.\n- Tokenpage harness: clean and one-field-mutated no-argument executions both checked zero studies. Explicit study naming detected drift. The numerical research was not falsified.\n- Spectral inertia: 860 exact matrices produced zero disagreements. The suspected naive-LDL singular-PSD crash did not reproduce. Both remain `N0` negative evidence.\n- Composed Gram certificate: a correctly bound singleton certificate falsely claiming zero norms was independently replayed and accepted at the reviewed head.\n- Combined controller study: all published verification commands passed, but four independent adversarial tests exposed trust-boundary and receipt defects.\n\nThe full `LEDGER.md` records source commits, exact hashes, commands, failures, limitations, and review IDs. `receipts/publications.json` latches one exact GitHub body match for each published review.\n\n## Preserved contradiction\n\nThe tokenpage prose log and independent machine receipt disagree on the unrounded no-legend empirical KL while agreeing on the with-legend value and rounded delta. Both sources remain unchanged. The ledger identifies the contradictory prose sentence as non-authoritative pending raw-input recomputation.\n\n## Integrity and portability\n\nThe manifest covers 132 files with byte lengths and SHA-256 values. Its own SHA-256 is `c3bf68d0f3171d48b17eff57a386de996835cf10e8c807f7d0470f540c5b6757`.\n\nOne spectral probe required a path-only portability edit for repository hygiene. Its original executed hash, published source hash, and a byte-identical replay are recorded. No scientific assertion or result changed.\n\n## Verification\n\n```text\nPYTHONPATH=src:. python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v\nRan 58 tests in 16.286s\nOK (skipped=1)\n```\n\nThat is 57 passes plus the optional live llama smoke skip. A prior invocation without `PYTHONPATH` failed during import and is retained in `receipts/final-verification.json`. The exact public-hygiene test also passes.\n\nChange request `6009446626` is answered in the ledger without rewriting trial outputs. The pinned raw QA file recomputes to `-6.651510759217704`. The 860 spectral matrices are 854 integer matrices plus 6 rational-cleared matrices. The naive-LDL note is limited to three small fixtures. Pull request 8 is now at `e7ea391c055b4f44aae93cc8f2e706d2ea488dbb`, and review `6009069465` is dismissed.\n\nThis branch also records change request `6009464930` on the hardening pull request at `e6ad0967c2386eb3e3bdc7d81ff3a47808d53a1e`. Further review is requested. Do not treat this PR as a merge approval or as live model evidence. No runtime code, Actions workflow, paid provider call, or external-organization write is included.\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-11-21T21:40:00Z","authors":[{"email":"342776047+orda-aska@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOFG5Y7w","login":"orda-aska","name":"Orda"}],"committedDate":"2026-11-21T21:40:00Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"research: preregister empirical iteration trials","oid":"3e2c8675514fe2d2b6b59706edf73f5cfa8e6273"},{"authoredDate":"2026-11-22T01:01:56Z","authors":[{"email":"342776047+orda-aska@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOFG5Y7w","login":"orda-aska","name":"Orda"}],"committedDate":"2026-11-22T01:01:56Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"research: preserve completed iteration trials and reviews","oid":"778d0062a538f7520a0644d08d9bfe554383087b"},{"authoredDate":"2026-11-22T01:45:31Z","authors":[{"email":"342776047+orda-aska@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOFG5Y7w","login":"orda-aska","name":"Orda"}],"committedDate":"2026-11-22T01:45:31Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"research: record the pull request 15 change request","oid":"ca8ced7bef75fe5a79435ea5f9aada3d80e820d6"},{"authoredDate":"2026-11-22T01:48:01Z","authors":[{"email":"342776047+orda-aska@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOFG5Y7w","login":"orda-aska","name":"Orda"}],"committedDate":"2026-11-22T01:48:01Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"research: narrow evidence wording after review 6009446626","oid":"516431afa21d53b98265aa8735f8a871707aad98"}],"files":[{"path":"research/iteration-2026-11-21/LEDGER.md","additions":149,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"research/iteration-2026-11-21/MANIFEST.json","additions":669,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"research/iteration-2026-11-21/PREREGISTRATION.md","additions":93,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"research/iteration-2026-11-21/lane7-review.md","additions":33,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"research/iteration-2026-11-21/pr12-combined-study/independent_qwen_recompute.json","additions":85,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"research/iteration-2026-11-21/pr12-combined-study/independent_qwen_recompute.py","additions":34,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"pa